<http://data.silknow.org/event/c4c4fe68-f525-3fce-9f4e-97cb0f89d186>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Copying an illustration from Konrad Gesner's Icones Animalium Aquatilium (published in Zurich, 1560). Embroidered at Sheffield Castle, South Yorkshire, by an unidentified member of the household of Elizabeth Talbot, Countess of Shrewsbury (Bess of Hardwick) (born, possibly at Hardwick, Derbyshire, 1527, died there, 1608).\n\nThe Oxburgh Hangings. Hanging with applied panels of embroidery, formerly at Oxburgh Hall, Norfolk."@en ;
        ecrm:P14_carried_out_by        <http://data.silknow.org/actor/d858d816-5ef4-3380-8e9e-1aff3f2527db> ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P23_transferred_title_from
                "Presented by Art Fund" ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/539ee952-7ca9-3aa0-b32c-518ded650a30> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Copying an illustration from Konrad Gesner's Icones Animalium Aquatilium (published in Zurich, 1560). Embroidered at Sheffield Castle, South Yorkshire, by an unidentified member of the household of Elizabeth Talbot, Countess of Shrewsbury (Bess of Hardwick) (born, possibly at Hardwick, Derbyshire, 1527, died there, 1608).\n\nThe Oxburgh Hangings. Hanging with applied panels of embroidery, formerly at Oxburgh Hall, Norfolk."@en .

